Here is the commit message:
bus: imx-weim: fix valid range check

When the range parsing was open-coded the number of u32 entries to
parse had to be a multiple of 4 and the driver checks this. With
the range parsing converted to the range parser the counting changes
from individual u32 entries to a complete range, so the check must
not reject counts not divisible by 4.

Fixes: 2a88e4792c6d ("bus: imx-weim: Remove open coded "ranges" parsing")
Signed-off-by: Lucas Stach <l.stach@pengutronix.de>
Signed-off-by: Shawn Guo <shawnguo@kernel.org>

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by a change in the parsing method for ranges in the `imx-weim` driver. The original implementation required the number of parsed entries to be a multiple of 4 due to the way entries were counted. However, after converting to a range parser, this requirement became invalid, leading to incorrect validation of the count of entries, which could now be any valid number rather than strictly divisible by 4.

Here is the patch:

 static int imx_weim_gpr_setup(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct device_node *np = pdev->dev.of_node;
 	struct of_range_parser parser;
 	struct of_range range;
 	struct regmap *gpr;
 	u32 gprvals[4] = {
 		05,	/* CS0(128M) CS1(0M)  CS2(0M)  CS3(0M)  */
 		033,	/* CS0(64M)  CS1(64M) CS2(0M)  CS3(0M)  */
 		0113,	/* CS0(64M)  CS1(32M) CS2(32M) CS3(0M)  */
 		01111,	/* CS0(32M)  CS1(32M) CS2(32M) CS3(32M) */
 	};
 	u32 gprval = 0;
 	u32 val;
 	int cs = 0;
 	int i = 0;

 	gpr = syscon_regmap_lookup_by_phandle(np, "fsl,weim-cs-gpr");
 	if (IS_ERR(gpr)) {
 		dev_dbg(&pdev->dev, "failed to find weim-cs-gpr\n");
 		return 0;
 	}

 	if (of_range_parser_init(&parser, np))
 		goto err;

 	for_each_of_range(&parser, &range) {
 		cs = range.bus_addr >> 32;
 		val = (range.size / SZ_32M) | 1;
 		gprval |= val << cs * 3;
 		i++;
 	}

-	if (i == 0 || i % 4)
+	if (i == 0)
 		goto err;

 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(gprvals); i++) {
 		if (gprval == gprvals[i]) {
 			/* Found it. Set up IOMUXC_GPR1[11:0] with it. */
 			regmap_update_bits(gpr, IOMUXC_GPR1, 0xfff, gprval);
 			return 0;
 		}
 	}

 err:
 	dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Invalid 'ranges' configuration\n");
 	return -EINVAL;
 }



